From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] samsung-sit: derive broadcast channels per country, not from one capture

The range table was this device's own Android capture written down, and
that capture was taken in Canada. 4396-4399 is not a default at all --
it is values-mcc302/additional_cbs_channels_strings. Shipping it as the
default would have been wrong for everyone outside one country.

Which cell broadcast identifiers a phone accepts is a property of the
*country*. It is not in carrier config, and it is not a modem property:
AOSP keeps it in res/values-mcc<NNN>/ overlays of its own
CellBroadcastReceiver, and 64 countries override something. The
assignment genuinely moves -- Brazil puts the monthly test on 4381 and
the exercise on 4382, where the default table has the exercise and the
operator-defined channel, and declares ETWS, presidential and AMBER as
explicitly empty, which disables them there. A single fixed list is
right in one place and wrong elsewhere, and being wrong here either
turns a test channel on or silences a real alert.

So tools/gen-cbs-channels.py generates src/cbs_channels.rs from those
resources -- the default table plus the 64 overlays, Android's own
overlay rule that a named category replaces the default and an absent
one falls back -- and default_ranges_for_mcc() assembles a config from
it: every identifier the country uses, accepted or refused by its
category, coalesced into the fewest ranges the CP needs.

That the derivation is right is not asserted, it is tested: MCC 302 has
to reproduce the captured 69-byte frame byte for byte, which it does,
from universal rules plus one overlay line. Every one of the 64 regions
is also checked to accept something and to fit the CP's limit.

ranges_for() replaces ranges_like_stock() and takes the country too,
since the refusals it spells out are the country's identifiers.

diff --git a/crates/samsung-sit/src/cbs_channels.rs b/crates/samsung-sit/src/cbs_channels.rs
--- a/crates/samsung-sit/src/cbs_channels.rs	1969-12-31 19:00:00.000000000 -0500
+++ b/crates/samsung-sit/src/cbs_channels.rs	2026-11-09 20:03:06.925321186 -0500
@@ -0,0 +1,932 @@
